/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Cache-Control is deliberately not set here. Cloudflare Pages serves the CSS
# and JS with max-age=14400 and the HTML with max-age=0, must-revalidate, so a
# returning visitor can get new markup and a four-hour-old stylesheet. That is
# how /ennova reached a phone unstyled while the same URL was correct
# everywhere else.
#
# Overriding it from this file does not work. Pages applies the rules above to
# /style.css and ignores a Cache-Control alongside them, which was checked
# against production rather than assumed. The fix is scripts/stamp_assets.py,
# which puts a content hash in the URL so a changed file is a changed URL.
